From: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: pass the netns to wireless_nlevent_flush()

Linux 7.4 made wireless_nlevent_flush() take the net namespace, which
is what mainline cfg80211 passes since then. Keep the argument-less
call for older kernels the backports still build against.

--- a/net/wireless/core.c
+++ b/net/wireless/core.c
@@ -1864,7 +1864,11 @@ static int cfg80211_netdev_notifier_call
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
 	}
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_GEQ(7,4,0)
+	wireless_nlevent_flush(dev_net(dev));
+#else
 	wireless_nlevent_flush();
+#endif
 
 	return NOTIFY_OK;
 }
